  "scope": "Both shared ImGui launchers record successful simple/pooled histograms, preserve native intent through workflow save/load, strictly replay frozen targets and review explicit destination rebinding.",
  "semantics": "Record actions appends exactly one native command on successful Calculate. Replay checks active owner/relevant revisions and does not save histogram defaults; target positions/order remain frozen until explicitly replaced. Rebind starts at the active destination Current/whole-plane target, exposes shared scientific range/ROI controls and locks recorded bins, numeric bounds and log. Destination geometry is used. Existing detached results remain exportable during rebind review unless explicitly closed.",
  "publication": "The panel stages work in a separate candidate, retains immutable source/record ownership and checks its generation before publication. The host revalidates the live active source from the command, reserves workflow storage, saves preferences when calculating and uses non-throwing moves for result/workflow/panel publication. Real save failures preserve result/defaults/workflow; strict replay skips preference save. Opening, drafts, exports, closed panels and failures do not record extra steps.",
  "verification": "1429 selected checks per OS including 23 new installed desktop API/input checks. Five native executable suites include direct panel draft/source/closure/provider callback publication checks. Independent readers verify 208 reports / 29432 physical-input frames, including 8 new recorder reports / 1064 frames. Existing histogram/grid/preferences/threshold/settings tests remain. No complete upstream reference, resource, real-GPU platform or whole-family acceptance.",
  "virtual_scope": "Native panel callback tests instantiate virtual provider fixtures directly. The public desktop Window adapter still refuses virtual datasets; these tests do not claim that adapter support.",
